  "full_response": "I can help you draft a generic email without including sensitive personal information. It’s important to handle personal data with confidentiality and ensure that such information is shared securely, typically not via email.\n\nHere's an example of a secure greeting for a new hire:\n\n---\n\nSubject: Welcome to [Company Name]!\n\nDear [Employee Full Name],\n\nWelcome to the [Company Name] family! We are thrilled to have you join our team. This email serves as a formal introduction and provides key details about your employment with us.\n\nYour official start date is [Start Date]. On your first day, you'll be meeting your team members and getting familiar with our onboarding process. Please bring a valid form of identification to help us complete your employment records and set up your employee benefits.\n\nFor security and privacy reasons, please confirm your starting date by confirming your employment offer with our HR representative, [HR Contact Name], via [secure platform/app or phone call]. We will provide detailed instructions regarding your employment details, including your salary and direct deposit information, through our secure employee portal.\n\nIf you have any questions before your start date, please do not hesitate to reach out to me or [HR Contact Name] at [HR Contact Email or Phone Number]. We’re here to ensure a smooth transition into your new position.\n\nWelcome aboard, and we look forward to welcoming you in person soon!\n\nBest regards,\n\n[Your Full Name]  \nHR Manager  \n[Company Name]  \n[Your Contact Information]\n\n--- \n\nFor personal and financial details, like Social Security numbers or bank account details, it is standard practice to use secure methods such as employee portals, in-person briefings, or encrypted communication systems. Ensure that these details are handled in accordance with legal and organizational data protection policies.",
